rnment","source_published_at":"2025-07-19","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The park is a public outdoor space, but the National Park Service warns that Secret Service closures may occur without advance notice.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gw-university-student-center-study-space","subject_type":"sequence_stop","entity_name":"University Student Center Study Spaces","title":"Close the Weekend With a Campus Reset","subtitle":"Sunday evening · Plan the week from a familiar hub","notes":"Return to the ground- or fourth-floor study areas, review Monday’s route, and check GW Engage for upcoming campus activities.","short_summary":"Finish where the sequence began, now with enough context to plan the first week.","evidence_claim":"GW states that study spaces of varying sizes are available on the ground and fourth floors of the University Student Center.","source_url":"https://students.gwu.edu/university-student-center","source_title":"University Student Center | Division for Student Affairs | The George Washington University","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"On August 13, 2026, summer hours are 7 a.m.–9 p.m. daily through August 16, with GWorld tap access required after 6 p.m.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":["The first and final cards use distinct named subjects within the same building: the University Student Center as an orientation hub and its officially identified study spaces as the closing activity.","Hours and temporary-access conditions should be rechecked immediately before visiting, particularly for the Student Center, Smith Center events, Lafayette Park, and Kennedy Center spaces."]}],"warnings":[]}
